Rotating a $4\times 4$ grid in place. Frames 2–4 transpose it one row at a time: each frame swaps the part of row $i$ right of the diagonal with the part of column $i$ below it (cyan), so only $6$ swaps are made and the diagonal $1, 6, 11, 16$ never moves. Frames 5–8 reverse the rows (green). The final grid's top row `13 9 5 1` is the old first column read upward — a clockwise quarter turn.

