#### Ring peel

::: {.form-next}
Iterate over rings instead of sides: `for k in range((min(R,C)+1)//2)` peels ring `k`, whose four walls are `k`, `R-1-k`, `k`, `C-1-k`. Walk its top edge, right edge, bottom edge (only if the ring has two distinct rows), left edge (only if it has two distinct columns). Same $O(mn)$ time, $O(1)$ space, and it is the version that reads like the picture of a spiral.
