    int m = board.size(), n = board[0].size();
    vector<vector<int>> old = board;
    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i)
        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {
            int c = 0;
            for (int x = i - 1; x <= i + 1; ++x)
                for (int y = j - 1; y <= j + 1; ++y)
                    if ((x != i || y != j) && x >= 0 && x < m && y >= 0 && y < n) c += old[x][y];
            board[i][j] = (c == 3 || (old[i][j] == 1 && c == 2)) ? 1 : 0;
        }
}
```
:::

#### Two states in one cell

::: {.form-next}
Drop the copy. Pass 1 reads only bit 0 (`& 1`) of the neighbours and stores the new state in bit 1 (`|= 2`); pass 2 shifts every cell right. The board itself is the copy, folded into the unused bit. $O(1)$ extra memory.
:::

